## Summary

The meeting was held on the 7--9th July 2025 at the University of Oxford, United Kingdom, in the Department of Engineering Science.

The format was similar to earlier Basilisk/Gerris meetings held in [Paris, France in 2011](https://gerris.dalembert.upmc.fr/gerris_users'_meeting_2011.html), [Wellington, New Zealand in 2012](https://gerris.dalembert.upmc.fr/gerris_users'_meeting_2012.html), [Sevilla, Spain in 2014](https://gerris.dalembert.upmc.fr/meeting_on_numerical_challenges_in_two-phase_flows.html), [Princeton, USA in 2017](BGUM2017), [Paris, France in 2019](BGUM2019) and [Paris, France in 2023](BGUM2023). Participants were encouraged to share their work using Basilisk (or Gerris) for applications in fluid mechanics, environmental science, engineering etc. Students were especially welcome to participate in this informal and friendly gathering.

The meeting was supported in part by funding from the Engineering and Physical Sciences Research Council IAA (Grant number EP/X525777/1).

